 "text": "Hey, how are you feeling? It means the screen shows you the current battery life as it drops, so you see how much time you have left. It depends on what you use your computer for. A typical desk computer can cause a power trip to trip if the screen drops too low. Yes, it does. The refresh rate tells your operating system to check the battery level more often, so it drains the battery faster. Then you probably want it set to something a bit higher than the default, but not so high that the icon is constantly swapping the percentage.",
